### Style + fonts wiring (2026-09-13)

`tokens.css` + `setpieces.css` + `brand-mark.svg` (style spec 1.1.0) and
the vendored WOFF2 fonts are snapshotted into this dir via
`pipeline/snapshot_style.sh` — a committed snapshot, not a live
`../pipeline/` reference. Two findings drove the mechanism:

- Render workers resolve CSS `url()` relative to the css file, and lint
  errors on any asset path climbing above the project root
  (`invalid_parent_traversal_in_asset_path`) — a `../pipeline/style/`
  link cannot work from inside the project.
- `<img src="….svg">` **works** (re-verified 2026-09-13 in a throwaway
  probe — no `media_load_failed`, mark renders). The earlier
  `media_load_failed` was a **misdiagnosis**: the real cause was that
  `brand-mark.svg`'s XML comment contained `--` (the token names
  `--paper`/`--seal-amber`), which is illegal in XML comments, so the
  file was malformed and failed to parse. Fixed the comment (no
  `--` inside comments) — the SVG is now well-formed and `<img>` and
  inline both render. Phase B rule: keep SVG XML well-formed (no `--`
  inside comments); either `<img src="style/brand-mark.svg">` or inline
  copy is fine.

Scene files import `style/tokens.css` + `style/setpieces.css`
(root-relative — base URL is the project root), e.g. the master
`index.html` does; scenes may do the same or rely on the master.

