Snapshot refresh 2026-09-13 (delete + re-snapshot, `snapshot_style.sh`):
first check run against a real scene exposed that the live browser in
check/preview resolves css `url()` relative to the css file, while lint
forbids `../` asset paths — neither a bare `fonts/` (404 at
`style/fonts/*`) nor a bare `../fonts/` (lint error) satisfies both.
Fix `167133f` (replacing `e9c70bd`): the snapshot copies the woff2 set
to BOTH `fonts/` and `style/fonts/` (byte-identical, `diff -r` clean);
one table above covers both dirs. Re-snapshotted from pipeline
`167133f`; `tokens.css` → `b0341f6d…` (banner text changed with the
fix); `setpieces.css` + `brand-mark.svg` + all woff2 byte-identical to
the table (values unchanged). Post-refresh: lint 0 errors/0 warnings,
check passed (runtime 0, layout 0, motion 0, contrast 7/7).

Wiring verified in a throwaway probe composition (not committed):
corner bug, hero number, bar-tag amber, `SEALED` stamp, inline brand
mark all render with the vendored fonts — proof frame
`snapshots/_probe3/proof-01-probe.png` (gitignored, re-derivable by
re-running the probe). `scan_theme_colors.py` over the project: only the
pre-existing `setpieces.css` rgba(107,112,120,.35) row-rule (ledger
border, pipeline-pinned) and the skeleton body `#000` (under every
scene's `--ink` background) need `--allow` — no scene-introduced drift.

