##### scene-04 fix — node-label centering + SCOREBOARD line collision (DRAFT, 2026-09-13)

Owner review of the committed scene-04 render flagged two nits; both fixed
in source (no timing changes — cues, reveal verbs, and draw durations
untouched). Spec amendments in `scene-specs/scene-04.md` (append-only
note on the SCOREBOARD sub-line and the Beat Timeline `every` row):

1. **Node labels left-aligned.** PREREG/SEAL/VERDICT/SCOREBOARD rendered
   flush against each box's left edge (measured: label text started 3px
   inside the box, ~130px of empty space to the right). Root cause was a
   shrink-to-fit flexbox no-op: `.node-label` had
   `display:flex; justify-content:center` but **no `width`**, so the
   absolute-positioned flex container collapsed to the text width and had
   no spare space to center within — lint, check, and motion all passed.
   Fix: give `.node-label` the box's explicit `width:240px`. Measured on
   the re-render (final frame): every label within 0.5–1.0px of its box
   center (PREREG 359.5/360, SEAL 759.5/760, VERDICT 1159.0/1160,
   SCOREBOARD 1559.0/1560).
2. **VERDICT/SCOREBOARD sub-line collision.** `judged by the pre-registered
   criteria` (centered 1160) and `every prereg in one public table`
   (centered 1560) were single lines on the same row (top 498) — ~390–400px
   wide each in 400px of center-to-center spacing → a 3px gap, glyphs
   kissing (measured 950–1348 vs 1351–1742). The two 400px-spaced columns
   can't hold two ~390px lines side by side, and the VERDICT line is locked
   in place by the three branch words stacked below it. The SCOREBOARD line
   is now two stacked centered lines, matching the pattern PREREG already
   uses: `every prereg in` (top 498) / `one public table` (top 532), both
   revealed on the same `every` cue (83.90 → 22.47 local). Measured on the
   re-render: clean 62–68px gap between `criteria` and `every prereg in`;
   `one public table` clears the `confirmed` branch (1102–1216) by 240px
   and the return-arrow rail (676) by 120px. Wording unchanged, no number,
   no data.

