##### scene-08 fix — bullet wrap-line alignment (DRAFT, 2026-09-14)

Owner review of the committed scene-08 render flagged one nit: on the
wrapped bullets the continuation line started at the card's left
content edge (under the `·` marker) instead of under the bullet's
first word. Fixed in the pinned set piece itself (not scene-local),
since `.disclaimer-card` is the §4.6 integrity anchor — no timing
changes: cues, reveal verbs, card geometry, and the 685 bottom are
untouched. Spec amendment in `scene-specs/scene-08.md` (bullet list
row). This is a pixel change to a pinned set piece, so style spec
bumped **1.1.1 → 2.0.0** (major; owner decision 2026-09-13 — this
review) and this video's style snapshot refreshed in the same commit.

1. **Wrap line sat 36px left of the first word.** The `·  ` marker
   (middot + one collapsed space = 2 chars = 2ch at the 30px mono
   advance) pushed line 1's first word to x=240, while the `<ul>`'s
   default padding dropped the wrapped line to x=204 (measured on the
   committed proof frame: line 1 L=240, line 2 L=204, delta exactly 36px).
   Fixed with a hanging indent on `.disclaimer-card ul li`:
   `padding-left: 2ch; text-indent: -2ch`. `W=2ch` is font-anchored
   (the marker is 2 chars in the monospace face) and pixel-identical
   to 36px in this engine (probe-verified; a 3ch control over-indents
   to 258). Line 1's width is provably unchanged — the negative
   indent returns exactly the padding it adds — so there is no
   reflow.

